    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (272 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string field to the `Owner` schema, alongside the existing `displayName`.\n\n2. **OwnerMapper** (`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`) \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of the first and last name, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\" +\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nSince the field is derived in the mapper (like the existing `displayName`), it's automatically returned on every owner response \u2014 including the create-owner response. The new `Cp07Tests` acceptance test (`initials == \"J.S.\"` for \"John S...\") passes, as do all 272 tests in the suite.",
